{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784647816,"nonce":"QYonzV7WtEIojURHrDmODRCyvb4=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nb4 pins the patchwork REST API to a single hardcoded version. The module\nconstant\n\n    PW_REST_API_VERSION = '1.2'\n\nis defined at `src/b4/__init__.py:79` and threaded into every patchwork\nrequest through one chokepoint, `get_patchwork_session()`\n(`src/b4/__init__.py:4941`):\n\n    url = '/'.join((pwurl.rstrip('/'), 'api', PW_REST_API_VERSION))\n\nEvery caller derives its endpoints from that URL — both the read path and\nthe write path:\n\n- **List patches (GET):** `pw_fetch_series()` →\n  `patches_url = api_url + '/patches'` (`src/b4/review/_review.py:3004-3042`).\n- **Update patch state (PATCH):** three sites, all building\n  `.../patches/\u003cid\u003e/` off the same `api_url` —\n  `patchwork_set_state()` (`src/b4/__init__.py:4982-4988`),\n  `pw_set_series_state()` (`src/b4/review/_review.py:3161-3172`),\n  and the TUI worker in `src/b4/review_tui/_modals.py:2668-2681`.\n\nThis explains the exact \"can list, can't update\" asymmetry the reporter\nsaw on patchwork.ozlabs.org: the collection query\n`/api/1.2/patches/?project=…` still succeeds there, but the per-patch\nresource `/api/1.2/patches/\u003cid\u003e/` returns HTTP 500 — and the state update\nPATCHes to precisely that per-patch URL. Under `/api/1.1/` the per-patch\nresource works. Because the version is a single hardcoded constant, the\nread path happening to work masks the write path failing.\n\n**No escape valve.** The version is not configurable — there is no\n`b4.pw-api-version` (or equivalent) config key; `docs/config.rst` exposes\nonly `pw-key`, `pw-url`, `pw-project`, `pw-discard-state`,\n`pw-review-state`. So a server whose 1.2 implementation is incomplete or\nbroken cannot be told to fall back, and there is no version negotiation\n(no probe of what the server actually supports).\n\n## Related bugs\n\nStandalone patchwork issue; no direct sibling among the tracked bugs. No\nfix suggestions per request.","files":null}]}